The manifests here describe models published by other people. Summo does not own
them and, for most of them, does not host them either — a manifest points at the
upstream URL, and the app downloads from there.

Two fields in every manifest carry the obligations:

  license         SPDX identifier for the model's own terms.
  attribution     Who published it. Required for attribution licences such as
                  CC-BY-4.0, and CI refuses a manifest that omits it.

A manifest may also set `redistributable: false`, meaning Summo may not host or
mirror the files. Those manifests must point at upstream only, and CI rejects one
that references a Summo CDN.

Models currently described:

  silero-vad-v5   MIT              snakers4/silero-vad
  whisper-tiny    MIT              OpenAI Whisper, ONNX export by csukuangfj
  campplus-sv     Apache-2.0       3D-Speaker (Alibaba DAMO), export by csukuangfj
